+## Summary
+
+Implement a dependency-free JavaScript state module and a small browser renderer. The three exported transitions are pure: they validate ids, create new arrays/objects for real changes, and preserve the original state for no-op paths. The browser bootstraps only when `document` is available, giving each item a native toggle button and enabling Approve only when a selection exists.
+
+## Technical Approach
+
+`web/app.js` will expose `initialState`, `toggleSelection`, and `approveSelected` through `module.exports` when CommonJS is available. State uses `items` and `selectedIds`; item status is always reset to pending by initialization, selection has no effect on a nonmatching id, and approval clears selection after mapping selected items to confirmed. The same module renders a small self-contained UI if `#review` and `#approve` exist. `web/index.html` provides the semantic container, heading, status output, and native disabled Approve button; inline styles give controls visible focus and pressed states without a missing design system.
+
+## Dependencies
+
+- Requires: Node’s built-in `node:test` runner only.
+- Provides: deterministic review-state functions for later capture/review work.
+
+## Testing Strategy
+
+- Unit tests: initialization, nonmutation, duplicate rejection, known/unknown toggles, selected/empty approval.
+- Browser integration: inspect rendered button attributes and disabled state in source-level assertions; no browser automation framework is present.
+- Contract tests: N/A; no network boundary exists.
+
+## Technical Context
+
+**Language/Version**: JavaScript, Node 24
+**Primary Dependencies**: browser DOM APIs; Node built-in test runner
+**Storage**: N/A
+**Testing**: `node --test web/app.test.cjs`
+**Target Platform**: modern browser plus CommonJS test runtime
+**Project Type**: small static web application
+**Performance Goals**: linear pure transitions; no network work
+**Constraints**: no external dependencies; browser use and CommonJS exports must coexist
+**Scale/Scope**: one module, one static page, one test file
+
+## Constitution Check
+
+No project or epic constitution, UX strategy, or design system exists. The implementation therefore uses semantic native controls, visible custom focus treatment, and no fabricated brand tokens. No architecture exception applies: this is a two-file browser feature following direct DOM patterns.
+
