+## Purpose
+
+This gives a reviewer a clear, reversible way to choose pending work before confirmation. It prevents accidental approval by keeping selection separate from the approval action.
+
+## 1. Experience (What the user lives)
+
+### 1a. JTBD Context
+
+**When** a reviewer is looking at pending items, they want to deliberately select the items ready to approve, **so that** confirmation changes only the work they explicitly chose.
+
+### 1b. Primary User Story
+
+As a reviewer, I want to select pending items and approve that selection so that I retain control over what becomes confirmed.
+
+### 1c. Felt Quality (How the user feels)
+
+| Surface | Entry emotional state | Target felt outcome | Banned feelings |
+|---------|-----------------------|---------------------|-----------------|
+| Review list | Careful and accountable | Certain about what will be approved | Surprise, accidental confirmation |
+
+### 1d. Magic Moments Tied to This Story
+
+No project magic moment is declared for this minimal project; `serves: []` intentionally makes no promise claim.
+
+## Functional Requirements
+
+- **FR-001**: System SHALL return fresh pending, unselected review state for an input list with unique ids and SHALL reject duplicate ids.
+- **FR-002**: System SHALL toggle selection only for a matching item id and SHALL leave state unchanged for an unknown id.
+- **FR-003**: System SHALL confirm only selected items, leave other items pending, clear selection after approval, and SHALL leave an empty selection unchanged.
+- **FR-004**: System SHALL render each selectable review item with a truthful `aria-pressed` state and SHALL disable approval until selection exists.
+- **FR-005**: System SHALL make the three required transitions available in CommonJS while preserving browser execution.
+
+## 2. Acceptance LARP (How we prove the experience works)
+
+### 2a. Required Personas to LARP
+
+| Persona | Flow | Build artifact | Evidence required |
+|---------|------|----------------|-------------------|
+| reviewer | select then approve items | browser page + CommonJS module | local tests and DOM inspection |
+
+### 2b. Acceptance Scenarios
+
+#### AC-1 — Pending review state is explicit
+- **GIVEN** an array of uniquely identified items
+- **WHEN** `initialState(items)` is called
+- **THEN** it returns a new state with every item `pending` and no selected ids
+- **EVIDENCE** Node test assertions
+- **VERIFIABILITY** agent-LARP
+
+#### AC-2 — Selection is deliberate and accessible
+- **GIVEN** a rendered pending item
+- **WHEN** a reviewer toggles its control
+- **THEN** only that item’s selection changes and its button exposes the matching `aria-pressed` value
+- **AND** the Approve control is disabled until one or more items are selected
+- **EVIDENCE** Node test assertions and browser DOM structure
+- **VERIFIABILITY** agent-LARP
+
+#### AC-3 — Approval changes only the selected items
+- **GIVEN** a state with selected pending items
+- **WHEN** `approveSelected(state)` is called or the Approve control is pressed
+- **THEN** selected items become `confirmed`, unselected items remain `pending`, and selection clears
+- **AND** an empty selection returns the original state unchanged
+- **EVIDENCE** Node test assertions
+- **VERIFIABILITY** agent-LARP
+
+#### AC-4 — Invalid identities do not cause silent corruption
+- **GIVEN** an unknown id or duplicate item ids
+- **WHEN** a transition is attempted or initial state is created
+- **THEN** the unknown id leaves state unchanged and duplicate ids are rejected
+- **EVIDENCE** Node test assertions
+- **VERIFIABILITY** agent-LARP
+
+## 3. Evidence Required
+
+| Evidence type | Required for state | Verifiable by | Path / convention |
+|---------------|--------------------|---------------|-------------------|
+| Pure transition tests | IMPL-GREEN | Node test runner | `web/app.test.js` |
+| Accessible control assertions | IMPL-GREEN | source/DOM inspection | `web/index.html`, `web/app.js` |
+
+## 4. Adversarial Cases (What must NOT happen)
+
+| Condition | Must NOT happen | Probe used to verify |
+|-----------|-----------------|----------------------|
+| Unknown item id | Any item is selected or changed | toggle unknown-id test |
+| Empty selection | Any item is confirmed | approval no-op test |
+| Duplicate ids | Ambiguous selection state is created | duplicate-id rejection test |
+| Browser rendering | `aria-pressed` diverges from selection | rendered-control inspection |
+
+## 5. Failure-Modes Handled
+
+| Dependency | Failure mode | Behavior | Verified by |
+|------------|--------------|----------|-------------|
+| Item input | Duplicate ids | Throw a clear validation error | Node test |
+| Item input | Unknown toggle id | Return original state | Node test |
+
+## 6. Related Tables / Surfaces (Cascade)
+
+| Write target | Related tables | Cascade behavior | Verified |
+|--------------|----------------|------------------|----------|
+| In-memory review state | Rendered review list and Approve button | Render reflects the newly returned state only | Node test/source inspection |
+
+## 7. Performance + Non-Functional Targets
+
+- Performance: transitions are linear in the item list and require no I/O.
+- Accessibility: native buttons, truthful `aria-pressed`, keyboard activation, and a disabled native Approve button.
+- Security/privacy: no persistence or external data handling.
+
+## 8. Data + API (Last, not first)
+
+### Key Entities
+- **Review item**: `{ id, label, status }`, where status is `pending` or `confirmed`.
+- **Review state**: `{ items, selectedIds }`; `selectedIds` is an array of ids selected by the reviewer.
+
+### API Surface
+- **`initialState(items)`**: validates unique ids and returns fresh pending state.
+- **`toggleSelection(state, id)`**: returns a fresh state with one known id toggled.
+- **`approveSelected(state)`**: confirms selected items and clears selection.
+
