+# UI Specification: Review selection state
+
+**Story**: S007-review-state  
+**Epic**: E001-capture-review  
+**Project**: 001-pulseboard  
+**Created**: 2026-08-10  
+**Version**: 1.0
+
+## Design Context Sources
+
+No project design system, UX strategy, wireframes, or active visual-test recipe exists in this workspace. This is a documented constraint, not a substitute for one: use a restrained editorial review surface with semantic HTML, high contrast, generous spacing, and clear control states.
+
+## PROFILE surface impact
+
+- [x] No
+
+## Visual Assets Requirements
+
+- [x] No
+
+## Component Overview
+
+**Component Name**: Review list  
+**Type**: Composite  
+**Design System Reference**: unavailable  
+**Affects**: static review page
+
+## Visual Specifications
+
+### Component Anatomy
+
+```
+Review page
+├── heading + concise instruction
+├── pending/confirmed item buttons (toggle selection)
+└── Approve selected button + live status
+```
+
+### Dimensions
+
+- Container: fluid, max-width 42rem, centred with 2rem page padding.
+- Review controls: minimum 44px height, 0.875rem internal padding, 0.75rem gaps.
+- Approval action: full width on narrow screens; intrinsic width above 768px.
+
+### Colors and Typography
+
+Use an ink `#17212b` on warm paper `#f7f4ef`, white item surfaces, and a deep teal action `#0b5d5a`. Selected items use a pale teal fill and 2px teal inset ring; confirmed items use reduced-contrast text with a `Confirmed` label. Heading is 2rem/700; body is 1rem/1.5.
+
+### Effects
+
+Controls use a subtle shadow and 12px radius. Hover raises the shadow, active lowers it, and keyboard focus uses a 3px `#f0a63b` outline with offset. Motion is a 120ms ease color/shadow change and is disabled under `prefers-reduced-motion`.
+
+## States & Behavior
+
+| State | Item control | Approve action | Accessibility |
+|-------|--------------|----------------|---------------|
+| Pending, unselected | white surface, `aria-pressed="false"` | disabled if none selected | native button label includes item name |
+| Pending, selected | pale teal, `aria-pressed="true"` | enabled | native pressed-state announcement |
+| Confirmed | muted, non-selectable | enabled only if other pending selections exist | text announces confirmed status |
+| No pending selection | unpressed controls | disabled | disabled native button |
+
+No form fields or asynchronous submission exist, so form validation, loading, and double-submit behavior are not applicable. A polite live status announces approval completion.
+
+## Interactions
+
+- Click/tap/Enter/Space toggles a pending item.
+- Click/tap/Enter/Space on Approve confirms the selected set once and immediately disables the action after selection clears.
+- Tab order follows reading order; focus is always visible.
+
+## Density Budget & Responsive Behavior
+
+- [x] Verified: one job—make a deliberate selection.
+- [x] Verified: one primary action—Approve selected.
+- [x] Verified: no secondary detail competes with the decision.
+
+| Target | Breakpoint/Device | Required | Notes |
+|--------|-------------------|----------|-------|
+| Web | 375px mobile | Yes | stacked action, 44px targets |
+| Web | 1024px desktop | Yes | centred readable column |
+
+## Accessibility Requirements
+
+- WCAG target: AA contrast and 44px touch targets.
+- Each selection is a native `<button aria-pressed>` whose value exactly follows state.
+- Approve is a native disabled `<button>` until a selection exists.
+- A `role="status" aria-live="polite"` region reports completed approval.
+
+## Implementation Guide
+
+- Render item controls inside `#review` from the returned state.
+- Keep `data-item-id` on item controls for event delegation.
+- Derive every visible state from `state`, never from stale DOM classes.
+- Put the action control in `#approve`; `app.js` owns its `disabled` property.
+
+## Testing Checklist
+
+- [x] `aria-pressed` is true only for selected ids.
+- [x] Approve is disabled with no selection and after approval.
+- [x] Keyboard-compatible native button semantics are retained.
+- [x] At 375px and 1024px the single-column layout remains readable by stylesheet inspection.
